{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101854} :activity/id #uuid "8d861dcd-02c5-53fa-858a-2be900cad05a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050163} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101854 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101952 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the following matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe denote the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}3$rd row and $\\color{red}2$nd column using the notation $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}.$\n\nThe first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column. So $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}=8,$ as shown below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{8} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can denote every entry of a matrix in this way.\nFor instance, $a_{{\\color{blue}4}\\color{red}1}$ denotes the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}4$th row and $\\color{red}1$st column.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "34f3a63d-a273-50fb-b26a-ae172c7e93e9" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2969 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "71c4da2c-9ba7-5b55-a1fc-62db722468f0" :step/math-academy-id 462030 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101855}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101855 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100988 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100683 :question/id #uuid "622baf41-fe35-55ee-bfc6-f1e6a2cb089a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4371" :question/problem "Find the entry $a_{23}$ of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry $a_{23}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and